A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 2Ki.25.23; 
son of: Hoshaiah (H1955H); also called Jaazaniah at 2Ki.25.23; Azariah at Jer.43.2; 
Another spelling of ye.zan.yah (יְזַנְיָה "Jezaniah" H3153)
§ Jaazaniah = "Jehovah hears"
1) a Judean, son of the Maachathite, a captain of the Judean forces who visited Gedaliah at Mizpah after Gedaliah had been appointed governor of Judah by…

A king of the tribe of Judah living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ki.13.2; 
son of: Amon (H0526H) and Jedidah (H3040); married to Hamutal (H2537) and Zebidah (H2080); 
father of: Jehoahaz (H3059H), Jehoiakim (H3079), Zedekiah (H6667H) and Shallum (H7967J)
Also named: Iōsias (Ἰωσίας "Josiah" G2502)
